That thing got me good.

263
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:23,633
What were you thinking?

264
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:27,060
Next time you do something
like that, warn me!

265
00:13:29,020 --> 00:13:29,900
Ah!

266
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:33,950
Soji!

267
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:45,440
It's coming!

268
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,540
It's not stopping!

269
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,897
The whole village will be swallowed up!

270
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:51,240
Get out of here!

271
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:54,980
We're going!

272
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,760
Koza, Krimanimo, get on!

273
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:00,540
Robson, serious moe!

274
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,070
Go!

275
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:04,300
Wapples, sir! Please!

276
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:06,057
You have to let us ride, too!

277
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:07,316
Get away from there!

278
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:09,440
You can all find your own way out!

279
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:12,650
Robinson, hurry!

280
00:14:12,733 --> 00:14:14,260
It's closing in on us!

281
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:19,929
We'll be all right!

282
00:14:20,012 --> 00:14:20,842
I promise, Phoebe!

283
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:25,097
Even if we get buried by this,
I'll be able to save you, I'm sure!

284
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:28,533
Bloofy and the others headed
up in that direction, right?

285
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:33,848
Do you think the avalanche could
have already gotten to them?

286
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,420
We gotta go faster!

287
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:19,637
Nami, I'm sure you're cold.

288
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,779
Just hang in there a little longer.

289
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:24,637
Listen, hang on to this for me.

290
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,191
I'll be right back, okay?

291
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:50,320
Oh, it was you guys in there.

292
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:52,872
No wonder it had such a disgusting taste.

293
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,419
I won't let him get away with this.

294
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:56,577
Who are you talking about?

295
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,837
You told me earlier that some of the Straw

296
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,977
Hats headed up the
mountain toward my castle,

297
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,060
isn't that right?

298
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:03,700
Then this happened!

299
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,137
They have a grudge against us.

300
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:07,577
They're still mad about what happened,

301
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:10,601
so they climbed up there
and started an avalanche!

302
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:14,740
So, they were the ones who caused it?

303
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:17,957
Those sinister Straw Hat
Pirates caused the avalanche!

304
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:18,870
That's right.

305
00:16:18,953 --> 00:16:20,260
Well, boys, let's go.

306
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,457
We'll see if those
stupid sea-loving sailors

307
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:24,952
know anything about fighting in the snow!

308
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:27,490
No!

309
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:24,517
I don't know what to do,

310
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:26,247
but I don't know what to do,

311
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:28,187
but I don't know what to do.

312
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:34,157
I'll get you there. Don't worry.

313
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,937
You just stay alive.

314
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:37,140
Both of you.

315
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:44,490
Up there!

316
00:17:44,573 --> 00:17:46,820
I see the brats up ahead, Wapbles, sir.

317
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,600
Found you!

318
00:17:49,780 --> 00:17:54,420
Now I'll make you pay, you damn Straw Hat!

319
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,070
Move it.

320
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,460
I don't think so.

321
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:07,707
Why would I want to do that?

322
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:10,357
I have no intention of
making it easy for you and

323
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,637
those half-dead friends of
yours to get away from here,

324
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:13,550
Straw Hat.

325
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:20,010
Hey!

326
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:21,620
Stop right there!

327
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:22,860
Ah, got it.

328
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:26,637
Hey, Chess, I've thought up a
new law to celebrate my return.

329
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:27,550
Write this down.

330
00:18:27,633 --> 00:18:28,463
Right!

331
00:18:28,546 --> 00:18:30,707
Anyone who ignores the
king will be executed!

332
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:36,013
Those three are guilty!

333
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:39,157
Chess, Karoo Marimo, I want
them to be punished immediately!

334
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:42,017
Deal with the two unconscious ones first
since they're ignoring me them all!

335
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:42,930
Sure!

336
00:18:43,013 --> 00:18:44,060
What did he say?!

337
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,617
I've got the woman on his back.

338
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:48,759
I'll take the man.

339
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:52,900
Prepare for Marmo's Surprise!

340
00:18:58,180 --> 00:19:01,768
Listen, Luffy, I don't want you
fighting these guys, alright?

341
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:04,977
Nami will be able to
feel every move you make.

342
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:07,477
She's too sick to be able to
handle something like that.

343
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:08,795
It would be too much.

344
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:09,940
She could die.

345
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:14,020
Can't fight!

346
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:20,500
You're gonna regret this
later, don't follow me!

347
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:22,260
Huh, what a coward.

348
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:23,780
It's no use!

349
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:34,240
It's time he learned what a
battle in the snow is like.

350
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:46,357
There's no one.

351
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:47,380
That's weird.

352
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:49,796
I wonder if they've already given up.

353
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,977
Here's what a snow battle's really like.

354
00:19:56,060 --> 00:19:58,354
Snow powder makeup, the white disguise.

355
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:02,619
Those two are so incredibly weak
that just one shot should be enough.

356
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:05,560
Now it's checkmate. No!

357
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:16,100
Polar bears?

358
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:21,130
Loppins!

359
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:26,020
Did those things just protect him?

360
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,097
That's impossible.

361
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:29,117
Loppins never form bonds with humans.

362
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:31,435
They're nothing more than wild beasts.

363
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,900
Thanks a bunch, you guys saved me!

364
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:50,580
Don't let him get away! Right!

365
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:05,769
What the hell are those stupid
bunnies doing standing there?

366
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:17,760
Doctor.

367
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:23,260
Doctor.

368
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:37,760
This is it.

369
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:41,380
It's tall and straight up.

370
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:50,680
But the doctor's up there,
so I gotta climb it.

371
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:55,120
All right, Nami and Sanji.

372
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:57,478
There's just a little further to go.

373
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,400
Oh, my God.

374
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,740
What happened?

375
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:51,900
The avalanche.

376
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:53,533
It must have buried us.

377
00:22:54,620 --> 00:22:55,450
Usopp!

378
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:01,060
Oh, there you are, Usopp.

379
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:02,377
Come on now, wake up.

380
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:03,800
You've got to wake up.

381
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:06,840
He's still alive.

382
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:09,057
I'm going to get you out
of there, Usopp, okay?

383
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:10,669
Just hang on a bit longer.

384
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:16,438
Come on, Usopp, please just wake up.

385
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:17,640
Snap out of it.

386
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:20,077
Just give me a few more
minutes here, Vivi.

387
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:21,817
I was in the middle of
such a lovely dream.

388
00:23:21,900 --> 00:23:23,737
We're in a world far away from here,

389
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:26,917
sitting in a field of flowers with a
beautiful river flowing next to it.

390
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,830
Oh!

391
00:23:27,913 --> 00:23:29,417
You're crossing over into
the afterlife, Usopp!

392
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:30,637
You need to get out of that dream!

393
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:31,550
Now wake up!

394
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,077
Ah, look at the Usopp pirates.

395
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,697
All 74,000 of them.

396
00:23:37,780 --> 00:23:39,437
They're such good, brave warriors.

397
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:40,640
Okay, get up now!

398
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:41,717
You have to wake up!

399
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:42,682
Do you hear me?

400
00:23:46,780 --> 00:23:48,297
Usopp! Usopp! Usopp! Usopp!

401
00:23:48,380 --> 00:23:54,688
Usopp!

402
00:23:54,771 --> 00:23:55,601
Usopp! Usopp!

403
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:56,514
You saved my life, Phoebe.

404
00:23:56,597 --> 00:23:57,427
I was almost a goner there for a second.

405
00:23:57,510 --> 00:23:58,340
I'm lucky to be alive.

406
00:23:58,423 --> 00:23:59,253
That was a close one, really so close.

407
00:23:59,336 --> 00:24:00,166
Except that my face feels kind of swollen.

408
00:24:00,249 --> 00:24:01,079
Why is that?

409
00:24:01,162 --> 00:24:01,992
Oh, it's the cold.

410
00:24:02,075 --> 00:24:02,905
That happens.

411
00:24:02,988 --> 00:24:04,457
It's an unfortunate side
effect of a snowy area.

412
00:24:04,540 --> 00:24:05,370
I don't know.

413
00:24:05,453 --> 00:24:06,283
Maybe it's the cold or something.

414
00:24:06,366 --> 00:24:09,037
What matters now is figuring out
where we are and what to do next.

415
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:11,296
Do you have any lip balm or anything?

416
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:16,530
Buster!

417
00:24:17,140 --> 00:24:18,820
Whoa, that was a close one.

418
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:22,136
Why do I feel like I dreamed
about a field of flowers?

419
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:26,237
Hit by an avalanche in the
middle of a training session.

420
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:30,908
Not exactly an ideal workout, but I guess
it is kind of like swimming in snow.

421
00:24:31,060 --> 00:24:31,890
Zoro?

422
00:24:31,973 --> 00:24:33,420
Oh, hey, VeeBee. What's up?

423
00:24:34,900 --> 00:24:35,730
Huh?

424
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:41,400
Oh, it's you, Usopp.

425
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:43,877
What are you guys doing all
the way out here in the snow?

426
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:46,607
That's exactly what we
were going to ask you!

427
00:24:48,180 --> 00:24:51,817
Take that you stupid bunnies you pathetic

428
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:53,837
creatures got exactly
what you deserve for!

429
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:57,597
Going up against the king still
it annoys me that I had to

430
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:01,237
expend so much of my power against
a pack of overgrown rabbits!

431
00:25:01,320 --> 00:25:05,673
There was no helping it sir they are
the fiercest animals in Drum Kingdom!

432
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:08,717
And you're next?

433
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:11,300
STRAWHEAD!

434
00:25:45,660 --> 00:25:48,460
argh !argh

435
00:25:56,220 --> 00:25:57,050
SAACHI

436
00:25:58,360 --> 00:26:04,457
!ARGH !ARGH !ARGH

437
00:26:04,540 --> 00:26:05,370
!ARGH !ARGH !ARGH!

438
00:26:05,453 --> 00:26:09,022
ARGH!

439
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,320
Oh, Lord.

440
00:26:14,420 --> 00:26:15,380
Winter swimming?

441
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,700
Yeah, that was the idea anyway.

442
00:26:18,020 --> 00:26:21,597
But after swimming in the river for a
while, I had no idea where I was anymore.

443
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:25,157
So I started walking around doing
some strength training workouts.

444
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:26,797
Dressed like that in cold weather?

445
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:28,197
You're real stupid, aren't you?

446
00:26:28,280 --> 00:26:29,257
That isn't the point.

447
00:26:29,340 --> 00:26:31,217
Now would you shut up and
give me your coat, Usopp?

448
00:26:31,300 --> 00:26:32,130
Not a chance.

449
00:26:32,700 --> 00:26:36,837
Maybe Nami's sick from the mental
exhaustion of dealing with these two.

450
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:38,037
And how about your shoes?

451
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:40,240
Nope. Just one, then. I said no.

452
00:26:40,420 --> 00:26:41,891
You did this to yourself.

453
00:26:42,460 --> 00:26:43,457
Look at that, guys.

454
00:26:43,540 --> 00:26:44,877
There's some people over there.

455
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:45,790
Huh?

456
00:26:46,460 --> 00:26:47,580
Uh, hey.

457
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,412
Look at those buildings.

458
00:26:49,540 --> 00:26:51,860
They seem familiar, don't they? Huh?

459
00:26:53,040 --> 00:26:54,216
You're right, Usopp.

460
00:26:54,380 --> 00:26:55,680
This place is Bighorn.

461
00:26:55,940 --> 00:26:57,100
We just came back.

462
00:26:57,300 --> 00:26:59,977
It looks a lot different
buried in snow, though.

463
00:27:00,060 --> 00:27:01,620
Stay back, all of you!

464
00:27:04,140 --> 00:27:05,905
Dalton's already dead, anyway.

465
00:27:06,260 --> 00:27:09,057
It'd take more than a couple
flimsy arrows to kill him.

466
00:27:09,140 --> 00:27:09,970
You're his men.

467
00:27:10,053 --> 00:27:11,097
Or used to be, at least.

468
00:27:11,180 --> 00:27:13,497
Don't you care at all about
what happens to Dalton?

469
00:27:13,580 --> 00:27:14,577
Things have changed.

470
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:16,317
We're all Wapol soldiers now.

471
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:19,417
And any one of you who opposes
Wapol is as good as dead.

472
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:20,817
Hey, what's going on here?

473
00:27:20,900 --> 00:27:22,135
What's going on here?

474
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:25,377
Wait, what's going on with you?

475
00:27:25,460 --> 00:27:27,225
Why are you dressed like that?

476
00:27:27,340 --> 00:27:30,877
Dalton is buried under the snow
that came down with the avalanche.

477
00:27:30,960 --> 00:27:31,790
What?

478
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:32,957
Dalton's under that?

479
00:27:33,040 --> 00:27:34,020
That's right.

480
00:27:34,300 --> 00:27:38,037
And we can't get over there to dig him
out because those guys are blocking us.

481
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:40,340
For the last time, stay back!

482
00:27:40,940 --> 00:27:42,917
But if you really want
to dig your friend up,

483
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:45,077
I guess you can go ahead
and try fighting us all!

484
00:27:47,020 --> 00:27:49,785
Hey, Ahusup, I think I
remember their clothing.

485
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:54,037
Those are the same exact guys who attacked
our ship when we were out in the ocean,

486
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:54,950
right?

487
00:27:55,033 --> 00:27:56,194
Oh yeah, that's right!

488
00:27:56,500 --> 00:27:57,557
Then they're the enemy!

489
00:27:57,640 --> 00:28:00,017
Bad guys, not our friends, you follow me?

490
00:28:00,100 --> 00:28:01,640
Yeah, but, wait a second.

491
00:28:01,840 --> 00:28:02,980
I know that look.

492
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:08,820
You aren't so brave without Dalton around.

493
00:28:15,540 --> 00:28:17,640
No! Zoro! What are you doing?

494
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:19,800
Who's that guy?

495
00:28:20,160 --> 00:28:21,513
You need to be careful.

496
00:28:21,740 --> 00:28:24,269
Nothing good will come
from attacking them.

497
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:26,800
This is so warm.

498
00:28:26,980 --> 00:28:28,451
I really like this thing.

499
00:28:28,780 --> 00:28:31,277
That's why you wanted
to know who they were?

500
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:32,301
Watch out, Zoro!

501
00:28:32,460 --> 00:28:33,757
They don't look very happy!

502
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:34,670
I know you.

503
00:28:34,753 --> 00:28:38,357
You were on the ship with that guy
who beat up Wapol, weren't you?

504
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:39,270
That's right.

505
00:28:39,353 --> 00:28:41,201
You're a little slow, aren't you?

506
00:28:58,360 --> 00:29:07,320
Whoa!

507
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:44,480
Hang on, you two.

508
00:29:44,920 --> 00:29:46,500
We're almost there.

509
00:29:47,460 --> 00:29:49,260
Don't you die on me.

510
00:30:00,100 --> 00:30:03,960
Oh, my God!

511
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:53,060
Oh, my God!

512
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:22,240
We're here.

513
00:31:32,300 --> 00:31:33,700
Doctor.

514
00:32:04,780 --> 00:32:05,610
Dr.

515
00:32:05,693 --> 00:32:07,951
Ine, the antibodies seem to be responding.

516
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:10,146
Yes, as I'd guess they would.

517
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:15,360
The treatment worked, but what
was the cause of the illness?

518
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:16,710
Kestia.

519
00:32:18,460 --> 00:32:20,284
Kestia, that's exactly correct.

520
00:32:20,540 --> 00:32:23,620
Now you go and attend
the girl, all right? Yes.

521
00:32:55,420 --> 00:32:56,820
Hello?

522
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:06,340
Oh, my God.

523
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:33,197
My life has been too still,
my heart is unfulfilled.

524
00:33:33,280 --> 00:33:37,180
But you could be the one to set me free.

525
00:33:39,540 --> 00:33:43,117
Something has to change,
my world can rearrange!

526
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:48,760
I'll do anything as
long as you are with me.

527
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:54,477
I've grown stronger having you by my side.

528
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:59,517
We've started on an everlasting ride.

529
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:04,380
I'm invincible when your love is near.

530
00:34:04,920 --> 00:34:09,480
When I'm with you I have no fear.

531
00:34:10,520 --> 00:34:15,797
Let's see how far we can make this go?

532
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:19,117
The world is ours.

533
00:34:19,200 --> 00:34:21,117
Use your pride I know.

534
00:34:21,200 --> 00:34:23,817
I see it shine.

535
00:34:23,900 --> 00:34:27,537
In the distance, glistening like water.

536
00:34:27,620 --> 00:34:31,660
When the sun rises in the dawn.
